**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A stack sample evaluated through Berreman, as the table solves it (001 §N 'stack samples go through Berreman (Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun for the table …) — REUSED'; 001 §I 'Sample by stack | the existing Sample …; unknowns may be a thickness'). Its thickness parameters (step 207) are applied to the stack and its materials are resolved once, when it is bound, so a sweep re-solves without re-resolving, as the host does today (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (1) `type ParameterValue with member this.thickness : Thickness`, the number read as metres, a `ThicknessParameter`'s unit (step 207's `Thickness.parameterValueOpt` is the other way). (2) `type Sample with member this.withThicknessValues (values : ParameterValues) : Result<Sample, ItemEvaluationError>`: after `values.checkedFor this.parameterAxes`, the sample with each finite layer's thickness replaced, every other field kept: the `SingleLayer` at film position k reads `ParameterName.filmThickness k`; layer j of the `Repeated` group at position k reads `repeatedLayerThickness k j`, the cell being stored once and shared by every period; the substrate plate reads `substrateThickness`; a `Thickness.Infinity` layer publishes nothing and is kept. (3) `ItemEvaluationError` gains `SampleMaterialErr of error : MaterialError` (a typed state, the store's own error), rendered `the sample's materials do not resolve: <the material error's reason>`. `BoundOpticalElement` gains `BoundStackSample of Propagation.ResolvedSample`, and `static member ofStackSample (materials : MaterialProxy) (values : ParameterValues) (sample : Sample) : Result<BoundOpticalElement, ItemEvaluationError>` is `withThicknessValues`, then `Propagation.resolveSampleMaterials materials` (`Propagation.fs:resolveSampleMaterials`), its `MaterialError` answered as `SampleMaterialErr`. (4) `muellerAt` on `BoundStackSample resolved` is `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun orientation.branch resolved w orientation.incidence orientation.rotation` (`Propagation.fs:sampleMuellerSpun`), both branches, the rotation being the sample's spin. No cache, catch or option is added; the solve is called as the host calls it today. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`, with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` (steps 45, 65): `a stack sample at its own thicknesses is solved as the table solves it`: for `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and `SampleIds.glassFilm200Id`, `ofStackSample` over `ParameterValues.defaultsOf sample.parameterAxes` evaluated at spin 20°, incidence 30° and 600 nm equals `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` of `resolveSampleMaterials` of the catalogue sample on both branches, element by element exactly. `a stack sample's thickness parameters change the layers they name`: on a test-local structure of a 5 nm `SingleLayer`, a `Repeated` group of a 10 nm and a 20 nm cell over three periods and a 1 mm substrate plate, `withThicknessValues` with `film1.thickness` 6 nm, `film2.layer2.thickness` 25 nm and `substrate.thickness` 2 mm answers those three thicknesses, the 10 nm cell layer and every material kept, its `expandedFilms` holding 25 nm in each of the three periods; a `film1.thickness` of −1 nm answers `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`; and `glassFilm200` bound with `film1.thickness` 300 nm evaluates, at normal incidence and 600 nm on `BranchTransmitted`, to `sampleMuellerSpun` of the resolved sample whose film is 300 nm, within 1e-12. `a sample whose material does not resolve answers SampleMaterialErr`: `ofStackSample` of `glassPlate1mm` over an empty in-memory material store (`MaterialStore.fs:MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty`) answers `SampleMaterialErr` of an `UnknownMaterialIdErr`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` covers `SampleMaterialErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the stack samples land, a sample bound at its own thicknesses MUST evaluate exactly as `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` solves it on both branches, its thickness parameters MUST change the layers they name, and an unresolved material MUST be `SampleMaterialErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a stack sample at its own thicknesses is solved as the table solves it`, `a stack sample's thickness parameters change the layers they name`, `a sample whose material does not resolve answers SampleMaterialErr` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.
